IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc6-smp`

-- Tests for ssc6-smp.l4 (Part XII, ss 164-171).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the Act's text (ukpga-1992-4.txt, lines 3241-3384),
-- beside the assertion. None is copied from what the code printed.
-- Numbers that regulations supply (the lower earnings limit, the prescribed weekly rate, the
-- prescribed duration) are arbitrary inputs here, chosen to put the test on each side of a boundary.
-- Dates: Sunday 4 January 2026 is `Day` 740289 (a multiple of 7); Sunday 8 November 2026 is 44 weeks later.

§ `Tests for Part XII`

§§ `Sundays`

#ASSERT (Day (Date 4 1 2026)) MODULO 7 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (Day (Date 8 11 2026)) MODULO 7 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (Day (Date 23 8 2026)) MODULO 7 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT ((Day (Date 7 11 2026)) MODULO 7 EQUALS 0)

§§ `s 164(2)(a) -- 26 weeks of continuous employment, and she has ceased to work for him`

-- The Act: "at least 26 weeks". 26 satisfies, 25 does not.
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(a) the number of weeks of continuous employment required` EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(a) she has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks and has ceased to work for him` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 26, 150, Date 3 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(a) she has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks and has ceased to work for him` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 25, 150, Date 3 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(a) she has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks and has ceased to work for him` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 52, 150, Date 3 1 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(a) she has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks and has ceased to work for him` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 26, 150, Date 3 1 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(a) she has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks and has ceased to work for him` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 26, 150, Date 3 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 164(2)(b) -- earnings not less than the lower earnings limit`

-- The Act: "not less than". Equal to the limit satisfies; one penny below does not.
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(b) her normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 30, 123, Date 3 1 2026) 123 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(b) her normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 30, 122.99, Date 3 1 2026) 123 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(b) her normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 30, 123.01, Date 3 1 2026) 123 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(b) her normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` (`Service for statutory pay` OF 30, 500, Date 3 1 2026) 123 EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 164(2)(c) -- pregnant, and at or past the 11th week before the expected week, or confined before it`

#ASSERT `s 164(2)(c) she has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(c) she has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(c) she has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(2)(c) she has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 164(2) -- the three conditions together`

#ASSERT `s 164(2) the conditions mentioned in subsection (1) are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(2) the conditions mentioned in subsection (1) are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(2) the conditions mentioned in subsection (1) are satisfied` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(2) the conditions mentioned in subsection (1) are satisfied` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(2) the conditions mentioned in subsection (1) are satisfied` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(2) the conditions mentioned in subsection (1) are satisfied` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 164(4) -- notice at least 28 days before, or as soon as reasonably practicable`

-- Arguments: gave notice; days before the date; not reasonably practicable to give 28 days; given as soon as practicable.
#ASSERT `s 164(4)(b) the number of days of notice required` EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` TRUE 28 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` TRUE 29 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` TRUE 27 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` TRUE 27 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` TRUE 27 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` TRUE 3 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` FALSE 60 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` FALSE 3 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 164(1) -- entitlement`

#ASSERT `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 164(3), (5), (6), (7)`

#ASSERT `s 164(3) the liability to make payments of statutory maternity pay is the person's` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(3) the liability to make payments of statutory maternity pay is the person's` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(5) the notice shall be in writing` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(5) the notice shall be in writing` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 164(6) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(6) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(6) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(6) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the agreement authorises deductions; authorised to make the same deductions from contractual pay; would be so authorised.
#ASSERT `s 164(7) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (6)(a)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 164(7) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (6)(a)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(7) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (6)(a)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 164(7) the agreement is protected from being void by virtue of subsection (6)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 165(1) -- the maternity pay period, at most 52 weeks`

-- 1 November 2026 plus 52 weeks (364 days) ends on 30 October 2027 (the last day is the 364th day).
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the longest maternity pay period in weeks` EQUALS 52
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` (Date 1 11 2026) 52 EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 11 2026, `the last day` IS Date 30 10 2027)
-- 1 January 2026 plus 39 weeks (273 days) ends on 30 September 2026.
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` (Date 1 1 2026) 39 EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 30 9 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` (Date 1 1 2026) 1 EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` (Date 1 11 2026) 53 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` (Date 1 11 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the maternity pay period if she were entitled to statutory maternity pay` (Date 1 1 2026) 39 EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 30 9 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(1) the maternity pay period if she were entitled to statutory maternity pay` (Date 1 11 2026) 53 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 165(2) -- the 11th week before the expected week of confinement`

-- The expected week begins Sunday 8 November 2026. The week before it is the 1st week before; the 11th week before
-- begins 77 days earlier, on Sunday 23 August 2026.
#ASSERT `s 165(2) the day on which the maternity pay period begins` (JUST (Date 8 11 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 23 8 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(2) the day on which the maternity pay period begins` (JUST (Date 15 11 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 8 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(2) the day on which the maternity pay period begins` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 165(3) -- a later prescribed start, but not later than the day after the confinement`

-- Arguments: the prescribed first day; the first day of the 11th week; the day she is confined (1 December 2026).
#ASSERT `s 165(3) the prescribed first day is permitted` (Date 2 12 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(3) the prescribed first day is permitted` (Date 3 12 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 165(3) the prescribed first day is permitted` (Date 24 8 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(3) the prescribed first day is permitted` (Date 23 8 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 165(3A) -- reduction of the maternity pay period`

-- Original 52 weeks from 23 August 2026 ends 21 August 2027. Reduced to 39 weeks it ends 22 May 2027.
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the maternity pay period as reduced` (Date 23 8 2026) 52 39 EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027)
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the maternity pay period as reduced` (Date 23 8 2026) 52 51 EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 14 8 2027)
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the maternity pay period as reduced` (Date 23 8 2026) 52 52 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the maternity pay period as reduced` (Date 23 8 2026) 52 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the maternity pay period as reduced` (Date 23 8 2026) 52 60 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: she would be entitled apart from the reduction; the first day of the week; the period before the reduction; the period as reduced.
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the woman would be entitled to statutory maternity pay for the week but for the reduction in the maternity pay period` (JUST TRUE) (Date 6 6 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the woman would be entitled to statutory maternity pay for the week but for the reduction in the maternity pay period` (JUST FALSE) (Date 6 6 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the woman would be entitled to statutory maternity pay for the week but for the reduction in the maternity pay period` NOTHING (Date 6 6 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the first week after the reduced period (23 May 2027) counts; a week starting on the reduced period's last day (22 May 2027) does not
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the woman would be entitled to statutory maternity pay for the week but for the reduction in the maternity pay period` (JUST TRUE) (Date 23 5 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the woman would be entitled to statutory maternity pay for the week but for the reduction in the maternity pay period` (JUST TRUE) (Date 22 5 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a week inside the reduced period, and a week after the unreduced period, are not weeks lost to the reduction
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the woman would be entitled to statutory maternity pay for the week but for the reduction in the maternity pay period` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(3A) the woman would be entitled to statutory maternity pay for the week but for the reduction in the maternity pay period` (JUST TRUE) (Date 22 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 8 2027) (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 23 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 22 5 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 165(3B) -- where the reduced period may end`

-- Arguments: the day the reduced period ends; the day she is confined (1 Dec 2026); the prescribed period (14 days) beginning with that day;
-- the last day of the unreduced period (21 Aug 2027); the prescribed part that must remain unexpired (28 days).
-- (a) "after a prescribed period beginning with the day on which the woman is confined": the 14 days end on 14 December 2026.
#ASSERT `s 165(3B) the reduced period ends at a time the regulations may allow` (Date 15 12 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) 14 (Date 21 8 2027) 28 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(3B) the reduced period ends at a time the regulations may allow` (Date 14 12 2026) (Date 1 12 2026) 14 (Date 21 8 2027) 28 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) "at least a prescribed part ... remains unexpired": 24 July 2027 leaves 28 days to 21 August; 25 July leaves 27.
#ASSERT `s 165(3B) the reduced period ends at a time the regulations may allow` (Date 24 7 2027) (Date 1 12 2026) 14 (Date 21 8 2027) 28 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(3B) the reduced period ends at a time the regulations may allow` (Date 25 7 2027) (Date 1 12 2026) 14 (Date 21 8 2027) 28 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 165(4), (5), (6) -- weeks of work`

-- Arguments: she works under a contract of service with the person in part of the week; the case is one prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 165(4) statutory maternity pay is payable by the person for the week` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 165(4) statutory maternity pay is payable by the person for the week` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(4) statutory maternity pay is payable by the person for the week` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(5) the work counts for subsection (4) whichever contract it is under` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(5) the work counts for subsection (4) whichever contract it is under` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 165(5) the work counts for subsection (4) whichever contract it is under` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: the week is after she has been confined; she works that week for an employer not liable to pay her; the case is prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 165(6) statutory maternity pay is payable for the week after confinement` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 165(6) statutory maternity pay is payable for the week after confinement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(6) statutory maternity pay is payable for the week after confinement` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 165(6) statutory maternity pay is payable for the week after confinement` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 164 -- the relevant week (seam S30)`

-- The expected week of confinement begins Sunday 8 November 2026. The 14th week before it begins 98 days earlier,
-- on Sunday 2 August 2026; the week immediately preceding that runs Sunday 26 July to Saturday 1 August 2026.
-- Arguments: a day in the expected week of confinement; regulations prescribe another period.
#ASSERT `s 164 the relevant week` (Date 12 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 26 7 2026, `the last day` IS Date 1 8 2026)
#ASSERT `s 164 the relevant week` (Date 8 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 26 7 2026, `the last day` IS Date 1 8 2026)
#ASSERT `s 164 the relevant week` (Date 14 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 26 7 2026, `the last day` IS Date 1 8 2026)
-- the next day starts a new expected week, and the relevant week moves a week with it
#ASSERT `s 164 the relevant week` (Date 15 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 2 8 2026, `the last day` IS Date 8 8 2026)
-- an expected week beginning Sunday 3 January 2027: 105 days earlier is Sunday 20 September 2026, 99 days earlier is Saturday 26 September 2026
#ASSERT `s 164 the relevant week` (Date 5 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 20 9 2026, `the last day` IS Date 26 9 2026)
#ASSERT `s 164 the relevant week` (Date 12 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 165(8) and s 171(1A) -- weeks`

#ASSERT `s 165(8) the week convention of subsections (1), (4) and (6)` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with the day on which a stated period begins`
#ASSERT `s 166(1A) the week convention of section 166(1)` EQUALS `any period of 7 days`
#ASSERT `s 171(1A) the week convention of Part XII` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`
-- A maternity pay period starting Sunday 23 August 2026: the week of Saturday 29 August starts 23 August; the week of Sunday 30 August starts that day.
#ASSERT `s 165(8) the first day of the week of the maternity pay period containing the day` (Date 23 8 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 23 8 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(8) the first day of the week of the maternity pay period containing the day` (Date 29 8 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 23 8 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(8) the first day of the week of the maternity pay period containing the day` (Date 30 8 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 8 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(8) the first day of the week of the maternity pay period containing the day` (Date 22 8 2026) (Date 23 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period starting Wednesday 2 September 2026: Tuesday 8 September is in the week starting 2 September; Wednesday 9 September starts the next.
#ASSERT `s 165(8) the first day of the week of the maternity pay period containing the day` (Date 8 9 2026) (Date 2 9 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2026)
#ASSERT `s 165(8) the first day of the week of the maternity pay period containing the day` (Date 9 9 2026) (Date 2 9 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 9 2026)
-- s 171(1A): a week begins on a Sunday. Saturday 7 November 2026 is in the week that began on Sunday 1 November.
#ASSERT `s 171(1A) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 11 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171(1A) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 8 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 8 11 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171(1A) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 9 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 8 11 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171(1A) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 166 -- the rate`

-- 90 per cent of 200 is 180.
#ASSERT `s 166(2) the percentage of normal weekly earnings` EQUALS 0.9
#ASSERT `s 166(2) the earnings-related rate in pounds` 200 EQUALS 180
#ASSERT `s 166(2) the earnings-related rate in pounds` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 166(1)(a) the number of weeks payable at the earnings-related rate` EQUALS 6
-- Arguments: the week number; normal weekly earnings; the prescribed weekly rate.
-- Weeks 1 to 6 are at the earnings-related rate (180); the prescribed rate 150 applies from week 7 because it is lower.
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 1 200 150 EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 6 200 150 EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 7 200 150 EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 52 200 150 EQUALS JUST 150
-- the lower of the earnings-related rate and the prescribed rate: when earnings are low the earnings-related rate is the lower one
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 7 100 150 EQUALS JUST 90
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 7 200 184.03 EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 0 200 150 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` 53 200 150 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 166(3): the prescribed rate must not be less than the weekly rate of statutory sick pay (the Act states 123.25 in s 157(1)).
#ASSERT `s 166(3) the weekly rate prescribed is not less than the weekly rate of statutory sick pay` 123.25 123.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 166(3) the weekly rate prescribed is not less than the weekly rate of statutory sick pay` 123.24 123.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 166(3) the weekly rate prescribed is not less than the weekly rate of statutory sick pay` 200 123.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 166(4): one seventh of the weekly rate.
#ASSERT `s 166(4) the daily rate of statutory maternity pay in pounds` 700 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 166(4) the daily rate of statutory maternity pay in pounds` 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 167 -- funding`

-- Qualifying payments of 1,000 are recovered in full; 92 per cent of the 1,000 that do not qualify is 920.
#ASSERT `s 167(2)(a)(ii) the percentage recoverable of payments that do not qualify for small employers' relief` EQUALS 0.92
#ASSERT `s 167(2)(a) the amount the regulations must provide for the payer to be entitled to recover in pounds` 1000 1000 EQUALS 1920
#ASSERT `s 167(2)(a) the amount the regulations must provide for the payer to be entitled to recover in pounds` 1000 0 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 167(2)(a) the amount the regulations must provide for the payer to be entitled to recover in pounds` 0 1000 EQUALS 920
#ASSERT `s 167(3) the payment qualifies for small employers' relief` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 167(3) the payment qualifies for small employers' relief` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 167(3) the payment qualifies for small employers' relief` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 167(6) the amount deducted is treated as paid towards discharging the employer's liability` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 167(6) the amount deducted is treated as paid towards discharging the employer's liability` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 167(6) the amount deducted is treated as paid towards discharging the employer's liability` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 167(8) the payment is a contributions payment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 167(8) the payment is a contributions payment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 167(8) the payment is a contributions payment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 168 to 170`

#ASSERT `s 168 Schedule 13 has effect with respect to the relationship between statutory maternity pay and the benefit or payment` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 168 Schedule 13 has effect with respect to the relationship between statutory maternity pay and the benefit or payment` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
